    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1017">

                <pb facs="0953" n="945" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg945"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense(M)/3366a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-09-20T14:00:00-04:00">September 20, 1941—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>162. Your 345, September 18, 1 p.m. has been repeated to London.<anchor n="31"
                        xml:id="d1017-f1"/> The Department has added that it is inclined to concur
                    with your suggestion but has instructed the Embassy to discuss the matter with
                    the British authorities and afford them an opportunity for comment <pb
                        facs="0954" n="946" xml:id="pg946"/> before action is taken here. A reply by
                        Tuesday<anchor n="32" xml:id="d1017-f2"/> at the latest has been
                    requested.</p>
                <p>Meanwhile, please inform the Turkish authorities that your Government attaches
                    the greatest importance to chrome and has the matter under urgent consideration.
                    You should if you find it necessary insist that the Turkish Government avoid any
                    agreement with Germany regarding chrome until we have had an opportunity to
                    present our views to the Turkish authorities.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
